---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";

// Google Play requires a reachable privacy policy URL for every listing, and
// because the apps serve AdMob advertising the policy must disclose that.
//
// TODO(owner): read this through and confirm every statement is true of your
// apps before you point Play Console at it. Where it says "we do not", make sure
// that is actually the case. This is a solid starting draft, not legal advice.

const updated = "4 September 2026";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Klica Technologies collects, uses and protects your information across our websites and exam preparation apps."
>
  <section class="section wrap">
    <div class="prose">
      <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="muted">Last updated: {updated}</p>

      <p>
        This policy explains how {site.name} (&ldquo;we&rdquo;, &ldquo;us&rdquo;) handles information
        when you use our website at {site.domain} and our exam preparation applications
        for Android and Windows (together, the &ldquo;Services&rdquo;).
      </p>

      <h2>Information we collect</h2>
      <h3>Information you give us</h3>
      <p>
        When you contact us, request an app or join a waitlist, you may give us your name,
        email address, phone number and the content of your message. We use this only to
        respond to you and to decide which apps to build next.
      </p>

      <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
      <p>
        Our apps and website collect limited technical information such as device type,
        operating system version, app version, approximate region and crash diagnostics.
        This helps us fix faults and keep the apps working across the wide range of devices
        our users have.
      </p>

      <h3>Practice data</h3>
      <p>
        Your practice scores and progress are stored on your own device so that you can
        track how you are improving. We do not upload your answers or your scores to our
        servers.
      </p>

      <h2>Advertising</h2>
      <p>
        Our free apps are supported by advertising delivered through Google AdMob and its
        partners. Advertising partners may collect and use device identifiers (such as the
        Android Advertising ID) and related data to select and measure the adverts you see,
        including personalised adverts where you have consented to them.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can review and reset your advertising identifier, or opt out of personalised
        advertising, in your device settings. Google&rsquo;s handling of this data is described in
        the <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Privacy &amp; Terms</a> pages.
      </p>
      <p>
        The authorised sellers permitted to sell advertising inventory in our apps are
        published at <a href={`https://${site.domain}/app-ads.txt`}>{site.domain}/app-ads.txt</a>,
        in line with the IAB app-ads.txt standard.
      </p>

      <h2>How we use information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To provide, maintain and improve the Services.</li>
        <li>To respond to your questions and app requests.</li>
        <li>To diagnose crashes and technical faults.</li>
        <li>To display advertising that keeps the free apps free.</li>
        <li>To comply with legal obligations.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Sharing</h2>
      <p>
        We do not sell your personal information. We share information only with service
        providers who help us operate the Services (such as our hosting provider, analytics
        and advertising partners), and where we are required to by law.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        Our apps are used by secondary school students, some of whom are under 18. We do not
        knowingly collect more personal information from a child than is needed to run the app.
        If you believe a child has given us information they should not have, contact us and we
        will delete it.
      </p>

      <h2>Retention</h2>
      <p>
        We keep correspondence for as long as needed to answer you and to keep a record of
        app requests. Practice data lives on your device and is removed when you uninstall
        the app or clear its data.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You may ask us for a copy of the personal information we hold about you, ask us to
        correct it, or ask us to delete it. Write to
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> and we will respond.
      </p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>
        We take reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect information.
        No method of transmission or storage is completely secure, so we cannot guarantee
        absolute security.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy. When we do, we will change the date at the top of this page.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        {site.name}<br />
        Email: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a><br />
        Phone: <a href={site.phoneHref}>{site.phone}</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
